# Sources added by this fork on top of upstream master 4e677cb6c6ab.
#
# The entry list below is the byte-exact output of the command under "Regenerate with".
#
# Regenerate with (base = 4e677cb6c6ab, the upstream commit this fork is based on):
#   { git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A 4e677cb6c6ab HEAD -- src include plugins tests/src/core tests/src/tracks \
#       | grep -E '\.(cpp|c|h|hpp|cc|cxx)$' \
#       | grep -vE '^(src/3rdparty/|plugins/NeuralAmp/rtneural/|plugins/NeuralAmp/nam/|plugins/NeuralAmp/tests/|plugins/RnnoiseDenoiser/rnnoise/)' \
#       | awk '/^tests\// && !/^tests\/src\/core\/(ClipSerialisationTest|DataFileSaveIntegrityTest|LufsMeterTest|MidiLearnTest|MixerConcurrencyTest|ProjectOpenIntegrityTest|SessionModelTest|StemExportTest)\.(cpp|h)$/ && !/^tests\/src\/core\/StemExportTestSupport\.h$/ && !/^tests\/src\/tracks\/SampleClipWindowTest\.cpp$/ { next } { print }' ; \
#     git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A 4e677cb6c6ab HEAD -- tools/local-ci.sh tools/ncpu-shim.c ; \
#   } | LC_ALL=C sort
#
# Verify it - this must print REPRODUCES and nothing else:
#   diff <(grep -vE '^[[:space:]]*(#|$)' tests/fork-sources.txt) \
#        <({ git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A 4e677cb6c6ab HEAD -- src include plugins tests/src/core tests/src/tracks \
#            | grep -E '\.(cpp|c|h|hpp|cc|cxx)$' \
#            | grep -vE '^(src/3rdparty/|plugins/NeuralAmp/rtneural/|plugins/NeuralAmp/nam/|plugins/NeuralAmp/tests/|plugins/RnnoiseDenoiser/rnnoise/)' \
#            | awk '/^tests\// && !/^tests\/src\/core\/(ClipSerialisationTest|DataFileSaveIntegrityTest|LufsMeterTest|MidiLearnTest|MixerConcurrencyTest|ProjectOpenIntegrityTest|SessionModelTest|StemExportTest)\.(cpp|h)$/ && !/^tests\/src\/core\/StemExportTestSupport\.h$/ && !/^tests\/src\/tracks\/SampleClipWindowTest\.cpp$/ { next } { print }' ; \
#          git diff --name-only --diff-filter=A 4e677cb6c6ab HEAD -- tools/local-ci.sh tools/ncpu-shim.c ; \
#        } | LC_ALL=C sort) && echo REPRODUCES
#
# The pathspec is `src include plugins` (this fork's product code) plus four extras the
# product command cannot derive on its own. Each is named here with its reason, so no entry in
# this file is a hand-edit nobody can account for:
#   * tests/src/core, tests/src/tracks - the pathspec's two tests/ additions (added with them,
#     not before) - this file holds exactly ten fork-authored TEST
#     sources (ClipSerialisationTest, DataFileSaveIntegrityTest, LufsMeterTest, MidiLearnTest,
#     MixerConcurrencyTest, ProjectOpenIntegrityTest, SampleClipWindowTest.cpp, SessionModelTest,
#     StemExportTest, StemExportTestSupport.h): three
#     registered by a42c68f24 (the integration fix that made Gate 9 green), two by 117068e76
#     (stem export), two landed at integration on 2026-09-12 from post-alpha/clip-slice0
#     (ClipSerialisationTest, SampleClipWindowTest.cpp), and two more arrived with
#     post-alpha/saveload-integrity the same night (DataFileSaveIntegrityTest, ProjectOpenIntegrityTest
#     - the lane registered them here itself, and they are kept rather than moved to
#     tests/all-sources.txt for the same no-narrowing reason), and one more arrived with
#     post-alpha/mixer-concurrency (MixerConcurrencyTest.cpp, registered by that lane here too; the
#     stale comment block it carried beside the entry claimed this command only walks
#     src/include/plugins, which stopped being true when the allow-list was introduced, and it is
#     dropped rather than kept as a false statement). They are the suites of fork-NEW
#     features, so the fork ratchets look at them. The other ~100 tests/src sources
#     added since the fork point are whole-tree material and live in tests/all-sources.txt only -
#     the awk filter admits exactly these ten. A new fork test source belongs in
#     tests/all-sources.txt by default; add it to the awk pattern above only if it must carry the
#     fork ratchets too, and then re-run this command.
#
#     Merged 2026-09-12 (integration wave 3A). The two clip-lane entries arrived on the
#     integration side of this merge and were hand-added there (their lane's own comment says
#     so); the gate-hygiene side, branched before that lane landed, could not produce them. They
#     are kept rather than moved to tests/all-sources.txt for the reason this file already
#     records for tools/local-ci.sh: the fork-scoped ratchets already measure them - including
#     tests/src/tracks/SampleClipWindowTest.cpp, which holds a fork file-length baseline entry
#     (511) taken by a recorded re-anchor - and moving them would narrow the fork scope. The awk
#     allow-list above was extended by exactly those two names, and the file now reproduces from
#     the command under "Regenerate with".
#   * tools/local-ci.sh and tools/ncpu-shim.c - the second, explicit pathspec line above. Both are
#     admitted by name rather than by widening the extension filter, because widening it also
#     admits five fork-authored .sh harness scripts under plugins/RnnoiseDenoiser/testdata/,
#     which would put shell tooling in the product scope.
#     - tools/local-ci.sh is registered HERE rather than in tests/tools-sources.txt because the
#       fork-scoped ratchets already measured it when that list was added, and moving it would
#       narrow the fork scope. Its reason is recorded in tests/tools-sources.txt's header too.
#     - tools/ncpu-shim.c was registered by the post-alpha/render-determinism lane (2026-09-12)
#       and is kept here at integration. It is a C source and therefore already on
#       tests/all-sources.txt's list (that list is `git ls-files` over the C/C++ extension set);
#       its presence here as well is what Gate 6 needs, because Gate 6 classifies a tools/ path
#       by tests/tools-sources.txt and consults no other list - registering it there instead
#       would be the same allowance by a different route, and the file is 93 lines with no
#       function over the complexity target, so the fork ratchets it widens are clean.
#       tests/tools-sources.txt's subtraction regex names it and does not repeat it.
#   * tools/stem-export-demo.py used to be a second hand-added tools/ entry in this file. It was
#     moved to tests/tools-sources.txt on 2026-09-12 (gate hygiene): tooling has one home, and
#     that list is the home tests/tools-sources.txt itself declares for tools/. It is not in the
#     command above any more, and this file no longer carries it.
#
# Why the base is a fixed commit and not `origin/master`. `origin` in this clone is
# upstream LMMS/lmms; this repo never pushes to it, and its `master` ref tracks whatever
# upstream publishes - on 2026-09-11 it was 518a7e8ef, which is NOT an ancestor of the
# fork point (verified: `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/master 4e677cb6c6ab` -> 1).
# The old command as written (`... --diff-filter=A origin/master HEAD ...`) therefore
# listed 116 files instead of 109: it reclassified seven upstream files this fork
# never authored as fork-new - include/AudioOss.h, include/AudioSoundIo.h,
# include/MidiOss.h, plugins/Sf2Player/fluidsynthshims.h, src/core/audio/AudioOss.cpp,
# src/core/audio/AudioSoundIo.cpp, src/core/midi/MidiOss.cpp - all of which exist at
# 4e677cb6c6ab (`git cat-file -e 4e677cb6c6ab:<path>`). The fork point is a fixed commit,
# so the corrected command needs no remote state at all. Verify it is in the clone first:
#   git cat-file -e 4e677cb6c6ab^{commit} && echo ok
# (`git merge-base origin/master HEAD` returns the same commit - 4e677cb6c6ab - but only
# while origin has been fetched; the literal commit is the base that cannot drift.)
#
# Vendored third-party trees are excluded on purpose (524 files): src/3rdparty
# (lua, luabridge), plugins/NeuralAmp/rtneural (RTNeural), plugins/NeuralAmp/nam
# (Neural Amp Modeler), plugins/NeuralAmp/tests, plugins/RnnoiseDenoiser/rnnoise
# (RNNoise). They are not this fork's code and these gates never refactor them.
#
# lcov extract patterns are anchored to the repo root (tests/run-coverage.sh
# resolves this file's directory to the repo root).
#
# The collation is pinned to C for the same reason tests/all-sources.txt's is: plain `sort`
# follows the caller's locale, so an unpinned command does not reproduce this file on a
# machine with a different one, and the tail entries appended by merge lanes ended up out of
# order for the same reason.
#
# Merged 2026-09-12 (integration wave 3B, merge #2 = post-alpha/brand-placeholders). That lane
# added four entries to this file by hand; NONE of them can be produced by this file's own
# command, so keeping them would make the file stop reproducing. Each is resolved by where its
# home actually is, and none is a silently dropped entry:
#   * tools/brand/rasterise-placeholders.py - MOVED to tests/tools-sources.txt, which is this
#     repo's documented home for the fork's own tooling under tools/ and whose own command DOES
#     produce it (the regeneration run reports it as the one added tools entry). Gate 9
#     classifies a tools/ path by tests/tools-sources.txt, so this is a recorded move of home.
#   * tests/brand-resource-sweep.py,
#     tests/evidence/brand-placeholders/verify-placeholders.py,
#     tests/evidence/brand-placeholders/provenance-audit.py - not registered in ANY scope, and
#     deliberately so: Gate 9's scope is C/C++ outside tools/ (is_source) and C/C++/Python/shell
#     under tools/ (is_tools_source), so a .py under tests/ is outside every list this gate
#     reads and needs no home. This file is the fork's PRODUCT scope - admitting test-side
#     scripts here would widen the fork-scoped file-length / complexity / duplication ratchets
#     onto them, which is exactly the scope widening 3A refused for
#     plugins/RnnoiseDenoiser/testdata/*.sh. Their commands are recorded in
#     docs/BRAND-PLACEHOLDERS.md and beside the scripts in tests/evidence/.
#
# Merged 2026-09-12 (integration wave 3B, merge #5 = post-alpha/racks). That lane added
# tools/rack-render-fixture.py and tools/rack-render-proof.py here by hand; neither can be
# produced by this file's own command, and the regeneration run proved it (both reported
# as `-` removals). Both are MOVED to tests/tools-sources.txt, the documented home for the
# fork's own tooling under tools/ and the list whose own command DOES produce them - a
# recorded move of home, not a lost entry, and the same treatment merge #2 gave
# tools/brand/rasterise-placeholders.py.
